hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1694","that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ""Whoever is pleased with Allah as (his) Lord, and Islam as (his) religion, and Muhammad as (his) Prophet, then he has tasted the sweetness of faith."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2623)"
"1695","A man said: Messenger of Allah, the mu'adhdhins excel us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Say (the same words) as they say, and when you come to the end, make a petition and that will be granted to you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 524)"
"1696","The supplication made between the adhan and the iqamah is not rejected. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 521)"
"1697","I have been given these last verses of Surah Al-Baqarah from the treasure beneath the Throne; they were not given to anyone before me, nor will they be given to anyone after me."
"1698","It was narrated from Abu Sa’eed that the Prophet ﷺ forbade building structures over graves. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1564)"
"1699","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'All the earth is a mosque, except for graveyards and Hammam.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 745)"
"1700","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""When you find only a sheep pen or a camel pen (as a place) to perform prayer, then perform prayer in the sheep pen, but do not perform prayer in the camel pen.\"""""
"1701","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: \""When you find only a sheep pen or a camel pen (as a place) to perform prayer, then perform prayer in the sheep pen, but do not perform prayer in the camel pen.\"""""
"1702","""The Prophet said: 'Perform prayer in the sheep's resting-places and do not perform prayer in the camels' resting-places, for they were created from the devils."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 769)"
"1703","The Prophet Muhammad said: ""There is a devil on the back of every camel. When you ride it, mention the name of Allah and do not fall short in fulfilling your needs."
"1704","“I was with Ibn ‘Umar and I lagged behind and prayed Witr. He said: ‘What kept you?’ I said: ‘I was praying Witr.’ He said: ‘Do you not have the best of examples in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?’ I said: ‘Of course.’ He said: ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Witr while riding his camel.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1200)"
"1705","The Prophet ﷺ said: Allah does not accept charity from goods acquired by embezzlement as He does not accept prayer without purification. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 59)"
"1706","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) wiped over his socks while performing ablution and he offered all the prayers with the same ablution."
"1707","""The Messenger of Allah used to perform ablution for every prayer, and we used to perform all of the prayers with one ablution."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 509)"
"1708","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed five prayers with the same ablution of the occasion of the capture of Mecca, and he wiped over his socks. ‘Umar said to him(the Prophet): I saw you doing a thing today that you never did. He said: I did it deliberately. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 172)"
"1709","She borrowed a necklace from Asma', and she lost it. The Prophet sent some people to look for it, and the time for prayer came so they prayed without ablution. When they came to the Prophet they complained to him about that, then the Verse of dry ablution was revealed. Usaid bin Hudair said: ""May Allah reward you with good, for by Allah, nothing ever happens to you but Allah grants you a way out and blesses the Muslims thereby."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 568)"
"1710","narrates: Once the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by him while he had removed the cloth from his knees, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cover it, for it is something that should be concealed."
"1711","Lady Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Allah Almighty does not accept the prayer of an adult woman without a veil (covering)."
"1713","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""When a person stands to perform prayer, he should tie his lower garment and fold it."
"1714","The Prophet Muhammad (pea"
"1715","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) stated that once people were offering the morning prayer in Quba. During thi"
"1716","""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Al-Madinah, he performed Salat facing the direction of Bait Al-Maqdis (Jerusalem) for sixteen or seventeen months. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ longed to face toward the Ka'bah, so Allah, Might and Sublime is He revealed: Verily, WE have seen the turning of your face towards the heave. Surely, We Shall turn your face in the direction of Al-Masjid Al-Haram (2:144). So he faced the direction of the Ka'bah and he longed for that. (One day) a man performed Salat Al-'Asr along with him."" He said: ""Then he passed by some people of the Ansar performing Salat Al-'Asr, while they were bowing toward Bait Al-Maqdis. He told them that he testifies that he performed Salat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he had faced the direction of the Ka'bah."" He said: ""So they turned while they were bowing."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2962)"
"1717","when the Prophet (May peace be upon him) turned towards the Ka’bah (in prayer), the people asked : Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him)! what will happen with those who died while they prayed with their faces towards Jerusalem ? Allah the Exalted, then revealed : “And never would Allah make your faith of no effect.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4680)"
"1718","narrates: My beloved (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) advised me regarding three things: To obey and follow (the ruler), even if he is a slave with mutilated nose and ears. When you make broth, add more water to it. Then look at one of your neighbors’ houses and give them a suitable portion from it. Perform the prayer at its (prescribed) time. If you find the imam has already performed the prayer, then you have protected your prayer; otherwise, (if you perform it again with the imam) your second prayer will be considered voluntary."
"1719","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: Perform the prayer at its (prescribed) time, then when you come to the people and they have already performed the prayer, you have protected your prayer, and if they have not yet performed the prayer, then perform the prayer with them, and it will be a voluntary (nafl) prayer for you."
"1720","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “There are two moments in which the gates of the heavens are opened: at the time of attending the prayer, and at the time of forming ranks in the path of Allah (while engaging in jihad).”"
"1721","The Messenger of Allah said: ""If you see a man frequenting the mosques, then bear witness to his faith. Allah says: 'The mosques of Allah shall be maintained only by those who believe in Allah and the Last Day. [At-Taubah: 18]'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 802)"
"1722","I instruct you to do good to your parents. He said: By the One who has sent you as a Prophet, I will surely participate in Jihad and I will leave these parents. The narrator states, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: You know better."
"1723","I seek Allah’s protection for you from the rule of fools. Soon there will come rulers; whoever goes to them, helps them in their oppression, and affirms their lies, he will have no connection with me and I will have no connection with him, and he will not be able to come to me at the Pond. And whoever does not go to them, does not help them in their oppression, and does not affirm their lies, he will have a connection with me and I will have a connection with him, and soon he will come to me at the Pond. O Ka’b bin Ujrah! Prayer is a means of attaining closeness (to Allah). Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sins just as water extinguishes fire. People go out in two conditions: a man trades his own self, so either he frees his neck or enslaves it. O Ka’b bin Ujrah! Such flesh will not enter Paradise whose growth is from the unlawful. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him), “He will have no connection with me and I will have no connection with him,” means that in regard to this action and this deed, he is not like me and I am not like him. These are the words according to the idiom of the people of Hijaz. His statement, “Such flesh will not enter Paradise whose growth is from the unlawful,” means “a specific Paradise” which will be other than another type of Paradise, because Paradise is of many kinds. Its example is like the statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him): “A child born as a result of adultery will not enter Paradise, a disobedient (to parents) will not enter Paradise, one who reminds others of his favors will not enter Paradise.” By this is meant one (type of) Paradise as opposed to (another type of) Paradise. This is a lengthy chapter; if Allah Almighty decrees and wills, we will mention it after this book (i.e., chapter) in a forthcoming chapter."
"1724","A man from among the people of Najd with disheveled hair came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The humming sound of his voice could be heard but what he was saying could not be understood. He came closer and it was then known that he was asking about Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Five times of prayer each day and night: He asked: Must I observe any more than them? He replied: No, unless you do it voluntarily. He (Talhah) said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned fasting during the month of Ramadan. He asked: Must I observe anything else? He replied: No, unless you do it voluntarily. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned Zakat to him. He asked: Must I pay anything else? He replied: No, unless you do it voluntarily. The man then turned away saying: I swear by Allah, I shall not add anything to this or fall short of it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The man will be successful if he speaks truth. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 391)"
"1725","The example of the obligatory prayers is like that of a river flowing at the door of one of you, in which he bathes five times a day."
"1726","""Do you think that is there was a river by the door of any one of you, and he bathed in it five times each day, would there be any trace of dirt left on him?"" They said: ""No trace of dirt would be left on him."" He said: ""That is the likeness of the five daily prayers. By means of them Allah erases sins."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 462)"
"1727","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) turned away from him. Then the prayer was established. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the prayer with salam, the man said, “O Messenger of Allah! I have committed an offense liable to a prescribed punishment, so establish it upon me.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, “When you came, had you performed ablution?” He replied, “Yes.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, “Did you pray with us?” He said, “Yes.”"
"1728","The narrator states) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not say anything to him. You called him and recited before him: “Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at some parts of the night. Indeed, good deeds erase bad deeds.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The Arabs sometimes mention a thing whose name consists of several parts and branches. Then the Arabs mention one of those parts by the name of the whole thing. All types of prohibited acts are forbidden for the servants. And the word “disobedience” applies to all of them. Among them is adultery, which makes the prescribed punishment obligatory upon its perpetrator. There are some causes that lead to it, so here the application of one cause is made to the whole act, and that cause is kissing and touching, not intercourse."
"1729","“And perform prayers at the two ends of the day and in some hours of the night. Verily, the good deeds remove the evil deeds. That is a reminder for the mindful.” [11:114] The man said: “O Messenger of Allah, is this (the Verse) just for me?” He said: “It is for whoever acts upon it among my nation.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4254)"
"1730","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent. Then Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: “Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at some hours of the night. Indeed, good deeds erase bad deeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.” The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called the man and recited this verse to him. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O Messenger of Allah! Is this ruling specific to him?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “(No), rather it is for all people.”"
"1731","The narrator named Abu Muhammad is Mas’ud bin Zayd bin Sabi’ al-Ansari, he belonged to Banu Dinar bin Najjar, he was a companion, and he resided in Syria.)"
"1732","The saying of Sayyiduna Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Abu Muhammad has lied,"" means he has said wrong. Similarly, it was the custom of Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that when someone said something wrong, it was said about him, ""He has lied."" Allah Almighty has protected the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from anything objectionable. The statement of Allah Almighty is: ""On that day Allah will not disgrace the Prophet and those who believe with him, their light..."" So when Allah has informed that He will not disgrace them on the Day of Judgment, then they are more deserving that no criticism be made upon them. The person who questioned Sayyiduna Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) was Abu Rafi’ Makhadji."
"1733","The five prayers and one Friday to the next Friday become expiation for the sins committed in between, as long as major sins are not committed."
"1734","I do."" Sayyiduna Abdullah said, ""If I had known him, I would have guided him to prolong his bowing (ruku) and prostration (sajdah), because I heard the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, say: 'When a servant stands to perform prayer, his sins are brought and placed upon his head or his shoulders, and when he bows or prostrates, they fall away from him.'"
"1735","""I met Thawban the freed slave of Messenger of Allah (S) and said to him, 'Guide me to a deed by which Allah benefit me, and for which Allah will admit me into Paradise.' He was silent for quite a while, then he turned to me and said: 'Perform prostrations, for I heard Messenger of Allah (S) saying: 'No worshipper performs a prostration to Allah except that by it, Allah will raise him a level, and erase a sin from him for it.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 388)"
"1736","""Angels come to you in succession by night and day, and they meet at Fajr prayer and 'Asr prayer. Then those who spent the night among you ascend, and He (Allah) will ask them, although He knows best: 'In what condition did you leave My slaves.' They will say: 'We left them when they were praying and we came to them when they were praying.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 485)"
"1737","""Angels come to you in succession by night and day, and they meet at Fajr prayer and 'Asr prayer. Then those who spent the night among you ascend, and He (Allah) will ask them, although He knows best: 'In what condition did you leave My slaves.' They will say: 'We left them when they were praying and we came to them when they were praying.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 485)"
"1738","""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'He will never enter the Fire, the one who prays before the sun rises and before it sets.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 471)"
"1739","My father said, ""Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever prays the two cool prayers (ʿAsr and Fajr) will go to Paradise.' "" (Using translation from Bukhārī 574)"
"1740","Abu Bakr bin Ammarah bin Ruwaybah narrates from his father: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say, ""The person who performs the prayer before sunrise and the prayer before sunset will not enter Hell."" One of those present asked, ""Did you hear this hadith directly from the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him)?"" He replied, ""Yes."
"1741","Sayyiduna Fadala bin Abdullah Laithi رضي الله عنه narrates: I presented myself before the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم. I accepted Islam and the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم taught me to perform the five prayers at their specific times. The narrator states: I asked him, \""These are the times when I am occupied. Please command me regarding something comprehensive.\"" The narrator states that the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم said: \""If you are occupied, then do not be negligent regarding the two Asr pray"
"1742","The Messenger of Allah taught us, and among what he taught us was also the explanation of what is meant by the two Asr prayers. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: The prayer before the rising of the sun and the prayer before its setting. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Dawood bin Abi Hind heard this narration from Abu Harb bin Abu Aswad and Abdullah bin Fadalah; he has transmitted the wording of both narrations, and both of its chains are preserved. The Arabs, in their language, mention things based on their quantity or abundance; they use the word ""before"" for a small thing, a long period, or a great duration. For example, regarding the signs of the Hour, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said that before the Hour, such and such tribulations will occur, even though these tribulations will be many years before (the Hour). This indicates that the word ""before"" is used for the meaning we have mentioned; it is not that the word ""before"" in the language is used to mean something being immediately adjacent. To the extent that (it would be ruled) that the morning prayer can only be performed just before the sun rises, and the Asr prayer just before the sun sets, while in this matter, the meaning of ""before"" in its entirety is intended."
"1743","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever performs the morning prayer is under Allah's protection, so O son of Adam! Fear Allah regarding this matter, lest He demand from you something that is under His protection."
"1744","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in praying 'Asr in Al-Mukhammas. He said: 'This prayer was enjoined upon those who came before you, but they neglected it. Whoever prays it regularly will have a two-fold reward, and there is no prayer after it until the Shahid appears."" And the Shahid is ""the star."" [1] [1] This is a statement of one of the narrators, and Allah knows best. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 521)"
"1745","The narrator says) This was the Asr prayer."
"1746","Messenger of Allah said: ""Salatul-Wusta is the Asr prayer."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 181)"
"1747","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, establishes prayer, and fasts in Ramadan, it is incumbent upon Allah to admit him into Paradise, whether he migrated in the way of Allah or remained where his mother gave birth to him."
"1748","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever performs the prayers, fasts in Ramadan, and avoids the seven major sins, for him the eight gates of Paradise will be opened on the Day of Resurrection, until it is prepared for him. Then he recited this verse: ""If you avoid the major sins which you are forbidden, We will remove from you your misdeeds."
"1749","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's prayer performed with the congregation is twenty-five times more virtuous than his prayer performed alone. If a person offers prayer in a deserted place, completes his ablution, and performs the bowing and prostration properly, he will receive the reward of twenty-five prayers."
"1750","The shine of the Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) ring is still before my eyes today."
"1751","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever remains in the mosque waiting for the prayer is considered to be in the state of prayer.”"
"1752","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): “Whoever waits for the prayer is considered to be in the state of prayer, as long as he does not lose his ablution.”"
"1753","O Allah, forgives him; O Allah, have mercy on him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 469)"
"1754","when the call to prayer is made; the devil turns his back and breaks wind so as not to hear the call being made; but when the call is finished, he turns round. When the second call to prayer (iqamah) is made, he turns his back, and when the second call is finished, he turns round and suggest notions in the mind of the man (at prayer) to distract his attention, saying: remember such and such, referring to something the man did not have n mind, with the result that he does not know how much he has prayed. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 516)"
"1755","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When the Iqamah for prayer is said, do not stand up until you see that I have come out.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 687)"
"1756","The best among you are those who have the softest shoulders during prayer."
"1757","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""There are three people whose prayer Allah does not accept: the imam of the people whom the people dislike, a woman who spends the night while her husband is displeased with her, and two brothers who are quarreling with each other."
"1758","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The one with the longest standing (Qunoot)."
"1759","I have not offered prayer behind anyone who performed the prayer more briefly and perfectly than the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1760","When one of you leads the people in prayer, he should be brief, for among them are the weak, the sick, and the aged. But when one of you prays by himself, he may pray as long as he likes. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 794)"
"1761","A man came panting to join the row of worshippers, and said: Allah is most great; praise be to Allah, much praise, good and blessed. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, he asked: Which of you is the one who spoke the words? He said nothing wrong. Then the man said: I (said), Messenger of Allah ﷺ; I came and had difficulty in breathing, so I said them. He said: I saw twelve angels racing against one another to be the one to take them to Allah. The narrator Humaid added: When any of you comes for praying, he should walk as usual (i.e. he should not hasten and run quickly); then he should pray as much as he finds it (along with the imam), and should offer the part of the prayer himself (when the prayer is finished) which the Imam had offered before him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 763)"
"1762","The distance between the Musalla of Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the wall was just sufficient for a sheep to pass through . (Using translation from Bukhārī 496)"
"1763","“Why do you not pray over there?” And I pointed to some corner of the mosque. He said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking out this place.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1430)"
"1764","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “There are two moments in which the supplication of the one who supplicates is accepted: when the prayer is established and when the ranks are formed in the way of Allah.”"
"1765","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him): I am astonished at an elderly man who, while leading us in the Zuhr prayer, said twenty-two takbirs. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas said: It is the Sunnah of Sayyiduna Abul Qasim (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1766","That Abu Hurairah used to lead them in prayer, and he said the takbir when he went down and came up. When he had finished he said: 'By Allah (SWT), I am the one among you whose prayer most closely resembles that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1155)"
"1767","Marwan appointed Abu Hurairah as governor of Al-Madinah. When he stood to offer an obligatory prayer, he would say the takbir, then he said the takbir when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing he said: ""Sami' Allahu liman hamidah, Rabbana wa lakal-hamd (Allah hears those who praise Him; our Lord, and to You be the praise)."" Then he would say the takbir when he went down in prostration, then he said the takbir when he stood up after two rak'ahs, after saying the Tashahhud, and he did that until he had finished the prayer. When he had finished his prayer and said the Salam, he turned to the people in the masjid and said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I am the one among you whose prayer most closely resembles that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1023)"
"1768","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began prayer with the takbir (Allah is most great) and with reciting “Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Universe”. And when he bowed, he neither raised up nor lowered down his head, but kept it between the two (conditions). And when he raised his head after bowing, he did not prostrate himself until he stood up straight; and when he raised his head after prostration, he did not prostrate (the second time) until he sat down properly; and he recited al-tahiyyat after every pair of rak’ahs; and when he sat, he spread out his left foot and raised his right. He forbade to sit like the sitting of the devil, and to spread out to hands (on the ground in prostration) like animals. He used to finish prayer with uttering the salutation. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 783)"
"1769","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to keep his fingers apart during prayer."
"1770","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Indeed, we, the prophets, were commanded to delay our suhur (pre-dawn meal), hasten our iftar (breaking of the fast), and hold our right hand upon the left hand during our prayers."""
"1771","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ started to pray, he would say Takbir, then say: ""Wajahtu wajhi lilladhi fataras-samawatiwal-arda hanifan wa ma ana minal-mushrikin. Inna salati wa nusuki wa mahyaya wa mamati lillahi rabbil-alamin, la sharika lahu, wa bidhalika umirtu wa ana min al-muslimin. Allahumma! Antal-maliku la ilaha illa ant, ana abduka zalamtu nafsi wa'taraftu bidhanbi faghfirli dhunubi jami'an, la yaghfirudhunuba illa anta, wahdini lihasanil-ahklaqi, la yahdi li ahsaniha illa anta wasrif anni sayy'aha la yasrifu anni sayy'aha illa anta, labaika wa sa'daika, wal-khairu kulluhu fi yadaika wash-sharru laisa ilaika ana bika wa ilaika ana bika wa ilaika tabarkta wa ta'alaita astaghfiruka wa atubu ilaik. (Verily, I have turned my face toward Him who created the Heavens and the Earth hanifa (worhsipping none but Allah Alone), and I am not of the idolaters. Verily, my salah, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, the Lord of the all that exists. He has no partner. And of this I have been commanded, and I am one of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the Sovereign and there is none worthy of worship but You. I am Your slave, I have wronged myself and I acknowledge my sin. Forgive me all my sins for no one forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of manners for none can guide to the best of them but You. Protect me from bad manners for none can protect against them but You. I am at Your service, all goodness is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I rely on You and turn to You, blessed and exalted are You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 897)"
"1772","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ started to pray, he would say Takbir, then say: ""Wajahtu wajhi lilladhi fataras-samawatiwal-arda hanifan wa ma ana minal-mushrikin. Inna salati wa nusuki wa mahyaya wa mamati lillahi rabbil-alamin, la sharika lahu, wa bidhalika umirtu wa ana min al-muslimin. Allahumma! Antal-maliku la ilaha illa ant, ana abduka zalamtu nafsi wa'taraftu bidhanbi faghfirli dhunubi jami'an, la yaghfirudhunuba illa anta, wahdini lihasanil-ahklaqi, la yahdi li ahsaniha illa anta wasrif anni sayy'aha la yasrifu anni sayy'aha illa anta, labaika wa sa'daika, wal-khairu kulluhu fi yadaika wash-sharru laisa ilaika ana bika wa ilaika ana bika wa ilaika tabarkta wa ta'alaita astaghfiruka wa atubu ilaik. (Verily, I have turned my face toward Him who created the Heavens and the Earth hanifa (worhsipping none but Allah Alone), and I am not of the idolaters. Verily, my salah, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, the Lord of the all that exists. He has no partner. And of this I have been commanded, and I am one of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the Sovereign and there is none worthy of worship but You. I am Your slave, I have wronged myself and I acknowledge my sin. Forgive me all my sins for no one forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of manners for none can guide to the best of them but You. Protect me from bad manners for none can protect against them but You. I am at Your service, all goodness is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I rely on You and turn to You, blessed and exalted are You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 897)"
"1773","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would begin the prayer, he would say the takbeer. Then he would recite this: \""I have turned my face, being upright, towards Him who created the heavens and the earth, and I am not among the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my life, and my death are for Allah, the Lord of all the worlds. He has no partner. I have been commanded of this, and I am the first of the M"
"1774","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the obligatory prayer, he used to recite: \""I have turned my face, being upright, towards Him who created the heavens and the earth, and I am not of those who associate partners with Him. Surely, my prayer, my life, my death, and my sacrifice are for Allah, the Lord of all the worlds. He has no partner. I have been commanded of this, and I am of the Muslims. O Allah! We are devoted to You."
"1775","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept silence between the takbir and the recitation of Qur’an. So I asked him, for whom I would give my father and mother as ransom: What do you say during you period of silence between the takbir and the recitation? He replied (that he said): O Allah, purify me from sins as a white garment is purified from filth. O Allah, wash away my sings with snow, water and hail. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 781)"
"1776","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept silence between the takbir and the recitation of Qur’an. So I asked him, for whom I would give my father and mother as ransom: What do you say during you period of silence between the takbir and the recitation? He replied (that he said): O Allah, purify me from sins as a white garment is purified from filth. O Allah, wash away my sings with snow, water and hail. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 781)"
"1777","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us in the mosque. He said: There are three things which the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to do, but people have abandoned them. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) would stand for prayer, he would raise both his hands, and before reciting (Qur'an), he would remain silent for a while in which he would ask Allah Almighty for His bounty, and during the prayer, every time he would go into bowing (ruku') and prostration (sajdah), he would say the takbeer."
"1778","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept silence between the takbir and the recitation of Qur’an. So I asked him, for whom I would give my father and mother as ransom: What do you say during you period of silence between the takbir and the recitation? He replied (that he said): O Allah, purify me from sins as a white garment is purified from filth. O Allah, wash away my sings with snow, water and hail. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 781)"
"1779","I seek refuge in You from Satan, from his prompting, his blowing, and his spitting."" The narrator named Amr says that by his prompting is meant epilepsy, by his blowing is meant arrogance, and by his spitting is meant poetry."
"1780","I declare the purity of Allah in the morning and evening.” Then he would say: “I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan, from his blowing, his spitting, and his whispering.” The narrator named Amr says: By ‘blowing’ is meant arrogance, by ‘whispering’ is meant epilepsy, and by ‘spitting’ is meant poetry."
"1781","""Abu Hurairah said: ""In should be recitation in every prayer. What the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made us hear (by reciting out loud) we make you hear, and what he hid from us (by reciting silently) we hide from you.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 969)"
"1782","The Prophet ﷺ said: ""There is no Salah for one who does not recite Fatihatil-Kitab."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 910)"
"1783","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person stands for prayer, he should not spit in front of him because as long as he is engaged in prayer, he is supplicating before his Lord. He should also not spit to his right side because there is an angel on his right. He should spit to his left side or under his foot and bury it."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration is a clear statement that it is obligatory for the follower (muqtadi) to recite Surah Al-Fatihah during prayer, because the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) has informed that the one praying is supplicating to his Lord, and supplication can only occur when someone is addressed verbally; reciting tasbih or takbir or remaining silent does not constitute supplication."
"1784","If anyone observes a prayer in which he does not recite Umm al-Qur’an, it is incomplete, it is incomplete, it is incomplete, and deficient. (The narrator said) I said: Abu Hurairah, sometime I pray behind the imam(then what should I do)? Pressing my hand he replied: O Persian, recite it inwardly, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying that Allah, Most High, has said: I have Me and the Half for my servant and My servant will receive what he asks. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Recite. When the servant says: “praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Universe,” Allah, Most High says: “My servant has praised me.” When the servant says: “ The Compassionate, the merciful, “Allah Most High says: “My servant has lauded me.” When the servant says: “Owner of the Day of Judgment,” Allah, Most High, says: “My servant has glorified Me” When the servant says: “ Thee do we worship and of thee we ask help. “ (Allah says) “This is between Me and My servant, and My servant will receive what he asks.” When the servant says: “ Guide us to the Straight Path, the path of those whom thou hast favoured, not ( the path) of those who earn thine anger nor of those who go astray,”(Allah says: ) “This is for My servant, and My servant will receive what he asks.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 821)"
"1785","""Messenger of Allah prayed the Subh prayer, and he had difficulty with the recitation. When turned (after finishing) he said: 'I think that you are reciting behind your Imam?'"" He said: ""We said: 'Yes, Messenger of Allah, by Allah!' He said: 'Do not do that, except for Umm Al-Kitab, for there is no Salat for one who does not recite it.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 311)"
"1786","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""There is no Salah for one who does not recite Fatihatil-Kitab or more.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 911)"
"1787","I do?” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When you stand for prayer, face the qiblah and say the takbir, then recite Surah al-Fatihah, then recite whatever you wish after it. Then when you bow, place your palms on your knees and keep your back straight. When you raise your head, stand up straight until every bone returns to its place. When you prostrate, perform the prostration firmly, and when you raise your head, sit on your left thigh. Then do this in every rak’ah of your prayer.”"
"1788","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prayer in which Surah Al-Fatihah is not recited is incomplete. Every prayer in which Surah Al-Fatihah is not recited is incomplete. Every prayer in which Surah Al-Fatihah is not recited is incomplete."
"1789","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""That prayer is not valid in which Surah Al-Fatihah is not recited.\"" (The narrator states: I said to Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): What if I am behind the Imam? He took my hand and said: Recite (Surah Al-Fatihah) in your heart.) (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In the narration transmitted by Alaa, the words \""the prayer is not"
"1790","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to recite Surah Al-Fatihah and to recite whatever (part of the Qur’an) is easy (for us). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says: The command to recite Surah Al-Fatihah during prayer is a command of obligation; the obligation of this command is established by other narrations, which we have mentioned in other places in our books. The command to recite “whate"
"1791","Go out and announce in medina that prayer is not valid but the recitation of the Qur’an even though it might be fatihat al-kitab and something more. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 819)"
"1792","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) led us in the Fajr prayer, and it became difficult for him to recite (the Qur'an). When he finished the prayer with salam, he said: ""You people recite behind me."" We said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Do not do so. Only recite Surah Al-Fatihah, because the prayer of the one who does not recite Surah Al-Fatihah is not valid."
"1793","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""There is no Salah for one who does not recite Fatihatil-Kitab or more.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 911)"
"1794","I said to Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him): If I am behind the Imam, so he took my hand and said: You should recite it in your heart."
"1795","from his father, from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever performs a Salat in which he does not recite Umm Al-Qur'an in it, then it is aborted, it is aborted, not complete."" He Said: ""I said: 'O Abu Hurairah! Sometimes I am behind an Imam.' He said: 'O Ibn Al-Farisi! Then recite it to yourself. For indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: Allah, the Most High said: ""I have divided the Salat between Myself and My slaves into two halves. Half of it is for Me, and half of it for My slave, and My slave shall have what he asks for. My slave stands and says: All praise is due to Allah, the Lord of All that exists."" So Allah, Blessed is He and Most High says: ""My slave has expressed his gratitude to Me."" He says: ""The Merciful, the Beneficent. So he says: ""My slave has praised Me."" He says: Owner of the Day of Reckoning. He says: ""My slave has glorified Me. And this is for Me, and between Me and My slave is: It is You alone whom we worship and it is You alone from whom we seek aid"" until the end of the Surah ""This is for My slave and My slave shall have what he asks for."" So he says: Guide us to the straight path. The path of those upon whom You have bestowed your favor, not those with whom is Your wrath, now those who are astray.""' (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2953)"
"1796","Concerning the saying of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime: ""And offer your salah (prayer) neither aloud nor in a low voice""- It was revealed when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was still (preaching) in secret in Makkah. When he led his companions in prayer, he would raise his voice"" -(One of the narrators) Ibn Mani' said: He would recite the Quran out loud""- ""And when the idolators heard his voice they would insult the Quran, and the One Who revealed it, and the one who brought it. So Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, said to His Prophet ﷺ: And offer your salah (prayer) neither aloud that is, such that the idolators can hear your recitation and insult the Quran; nor in a low voice, so that your companions cannot hear; but follow a way between."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1011)"
"1797","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), so he recited « » , then recited Surah Al-Fatihah, until when he finished reciting « » , he said Ameen; the people also said Ameen. When he went into ruku, he said Allahu Akbar. When he raised his head, he said « » , then he said « » . Then when he went into prostration, he said « » , and when he raised his head, he said « » . Then, saying Takbeer, he stood up straight. When he stood up after performing two rak'ahs, he said « » . Then, when he finished the prayer with salam, he said: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I am the one among you who most closely resembles the prayer of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1798","The Prophet(peace be upon hm), Abu Bakr, ‘Umar and ‘Uthman used to begin the recitation with “Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Universe.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 782)"
"1799","""I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, and I did not hear any of them say out loud: In the Name of Allah, The Most Gracious, The Most Merciful."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 907)"
"1800","The Prophet(peace be upon hm), Abu Bakr, ‘Umar and ‘Uthman used to begin the recitation with “Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Universe.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 782)"
"1801","""I prayed behind Abu Hurairah and he recited: In the Name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, then he recited Umm Al-Qur'an (Al Fatihah), and when he reached: not (the way) of those who earned Your anger, nor of those who went astray, he said: 'Amin and the people said 'Amin. And every time he prostrated he said: 'Allahu Akbar and when he stood up from sitting after two Rak'ahs he said: 'Allahu Akbar'. And after he had said the Salam he said: 'By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! My prayer most closely remembers the prayer of the Messenger of Allah.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 905)"
"1802","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) did not recite « » in a loud voice."
"1803","narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) did not recite « » aloud. These noble ones used to recite « » aloud."
"1804","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When the Imam says: Not (the way) of those who earned Your anger, nor of those who went astray, say: 'Amin' for the angels say Amin and the Imam says Amin, and if a person's Amin coincides with the Amin of the angels, his previous sins will be forgiven.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 927)"
"1805","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his right blessed hand over his left blessed hand. When he said « » , he said Ameen. At the end of the prayer, he turned (for salam) to his right side and to his left side (i.e., twice)."
"1806","narrates that when the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, finished the recitation of Surah Al-Fatihah, he would say ""Ameen"" aloud."
"1807","The narrator says) I mentioned this to Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him), so he said to me: I only remember him remaining silent at one occasion. Then we wrote a letter regarding this to Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) in Madinah Munawwarah. He replied: Sayyiduna Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) remembers this matter correctly. The narrator named Sa'id says: We asked Qatadah: What were these two occasions of silence? He said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would begin the prayer, and when he would finish the recitation. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Hasan did not hear anything from Sayyiduna Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him). He heard this narration from Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him), and in this matter, our reliance is upon the narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Imran (may Allah be pleased with him), not the one transmitted from Sayyiduna Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1808","I think these words are also in the narration:"" « » . (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Yazid Abu Khalid is Yazid bin Abdur Rahman Dalani Abu Khalid."
